[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 500,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 539,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69299,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 243,
        "headingId": 539,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Renal haemangioblastoma is similar to haemangioblastoma of the CNS and composed of capillaries and stromal cells. Unlike CNS tumours, renal haemangioblastomas are not associated with von Hippel&ndash;Lindau syndrome.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:59:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 501,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 540,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69300,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 243,
        "headingId": 540,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9161/1 Haemangioblastoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:59:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 502,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 541,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69301,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 243,
        "headingId": 541,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F98 &amp; XH6810 Neoplasms of unknown behaviour of urinary organs &amp; Haemangioblastoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:59:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 503,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 542,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69302,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 243,
        "headingId": 542,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:59:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 504,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 543,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69303,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 243,
        "headingId": 543,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:59:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69304,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 243,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Any renal location</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:59:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69305,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 243,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Renal haemangioblastomas have been reported only in adults (patient age range: 29&ndash;71&nbsp;years). Most patients are asymptomatic, but haematuria and abdominal/back pain have occurred. Imaging characteristics cannot distinguish renal haemangioblastomas from renal epithelial tumours {31893030}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:59:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69306,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 243,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fewer than 15&nbsp;cases have been reported. Tumours occur in adults and there is an equal sex distribution. No predisposing conditions have been identified {31893030; 29941223}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:59:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69307,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 243,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is no known etiology. The tumours are not associated with von Hippel&ndash;Lindau syndrome {29941223}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:59:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69308,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 243,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:59:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69309,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 243,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours range from 120 to 680&nbsp;mm in greatest dimension {31893030}. They are encapsulated, they may be red-brown, grey, and/or yellow, and some tumours show areas of haemorrhage {22497861; 22271882; 26201545; 22548972}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:59:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69310,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 243,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours are well circumscribed, and they are composed of sheets of cells with round to oval nuclei and clear to slightly eosinophilic cytoplasm. The clear cytoplasm may be vacuolated as a result of lipid accumulation. Additionally, cytoplasmic eosinophilic globules may be present. There may be mild cytological atypia with scattered larger cells, but diffuse atypia is not present. Rhabdoid features have been described {31893050; 22497861}. The neoplastic cells are associated with a network of arborizing thin-walled capillaries. Mitotic activity is very low. Necrosis has been reported in a minority of cases.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>Immunohistochemical findings show staining for PAX8, &alpha;-inhibin, NSE, S100, and vimentin {23849894; 25973115; 12883249}. CAIX and partial CD10 membrane staining has been reported {25973115}. There may be focal EMA and cytokeratin staining, but cytokeratins are usually negative, as are chromogranin, synaptophysin, and melanocytic markers other than S100.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:59:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69311,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 243,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:59:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 551,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69312,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 243,
        "headingId": 551,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There are no diagnostic molecular abnormalities. These tumours lack alterations of <em>VHL</em>.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:59:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 515,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 554,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69313,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 243,
        "headingId": 554,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> cells with round to oval nuclei with clear to slightly eosinophilic cytoplasm set in a background of arborizing capillaries.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> immunophenotyping shows positivity for PAX8, S100, and &alpha;-inhibin, and usually negativity for keratin.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:59:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 513,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 552,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69314,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 243,
        "headingId": 552,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most tumours are pT1 or (rarely) pT2, with an absence of renal sinus, perinephric fat, and renal vein invasion. Regional lymph node involvement is not reported.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:59:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 514,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 553,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69315,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 243,
        "headingId": 553,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>No tumours have been reported to recur or metastasize {31893050}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:59:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]